course: dictionary
lesson: 8799
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word sharply is a good example. «When it turns sharply, you lurch outwards» means the turn is sudden and steep. «Speak sharply to someone» would mean something quite different.
explain: Look for clues in the words around sharply. Words like turn, rise, drop, focus, or speaking tell you which meaning fits. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sharply is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens: how a road turns, how a price rises, how someone speaks, or how clear a picture is. Ask yourself "how?" and the words next to sharply will help you find the answer.
fact: Sharply can mean suddenly and by a lot, as in «turn sharply» or «rise sharply».
fact: Sharply can mean in an angry or strict way, as in «speaking sharply to someone».
fact: Sharply can mean very clearly, as in «a picture that is sharply in focus».
fact: In graphs, a line that rises or falls sharply goes up or down steeply and quickly.
fact: «Sharply dressed» means smart.
exercise: «When it turns sharply, you lurch outwards.» What does sharply mean in this sentence? | Smoothly and slowly | *Suddenly and by a lot, so the turn is quick and steep | Very clearly, in focus | Crossly, in an angry voice
exercise: Dad says, «Don't speak to me so sharply!» What does sharply mean here? | Very clearly | Quietly and softly | *In an angry or strict way | With a sharp point or edge
exercise: «The photo was sharply in focus.» What does sharply mean here? | *Very clearly | With a point | Crossly, with an angry tone | Suddenly and by a lot
test: «Ostriches ... turn sharply when running.» What does turn sharply suggest? | *Change direction quickly and by a lot | Fall over slowly | Speak crossly to the other birds | Stand still and wait
test: «Roast» in young slang means to make fun of someone sharply. What does sharply mean in that sentence? | *In a harsh, cutting way | Very clearly | Suddenly and by a lot | Slowly and kindly
exam: «The temperature began to drop sharply overnight.» What does sharply mean? | Very clearly | *Suddenly and by a lot | Angrily, in a loud voice | Slowly and gently
